(Stage 1b safety. Reading an element out of a list that widened to Mixed
 yields a value whose type the compiler cannot prove. A declared type on
 the receiving variable states the author's intent, not what the slot
 holds, so it must not be turned into a slot tag: writing TAG_STRING over
 the integer 42 made the tag-dispatching printer treat 42 as a C-string
 pointer and dereference it - a segfault, which no valid Vox program may
 do. The pre-scan marks such values unprovable and the write falls back to
 the integer tag, which renders as a number and never dereferences.)

a list called "m" is ["a", "b"].
append 42 to m.
a text called "s" is element 3 of m.
a list called "out" is [].
append s to out.
print m.
print out.
